                "block_type": "paragraph",
                "text": "Apply the same one-step acceleration-to-velocity model to $a(t)=2t$ with $v(0)=-2$. Write the explicit signal $v(t)$.",
                "latex": "",
                "image_slot_id": ""
              }
            ],
            "choices": [],
            "correct_choice_labels": [],
            "correct_answer": "$v(t)=t^2-2$",
            "answer_explanation_blocks": [
              {
                "block_type": "paragraph",
                "text": "Use $v(t)=\\int_{0}^{t} a(\\tau)\\,d\\tau+v(0)$. For $a(\\tau)=2\\tau$, integration gives $\\int_{0}^{t}2\\tau\\,d\\tau=t^2$, then include $v(0)=-2$, so $v(t)=t^2-2$.",
                "latex": "",
                "image_slot_id": ""
              }
            ]
          }
        ]
      },
      {
